    "changes": "Remove crowded upper attacks while preserving all four companion phrases and later bloom. Join closing/opening F# minor voicing through sustained lower tones; remove high closing bell and fresh opening bass/pad/arpeggio reattacks. Remaining bell entrances vary by 26\u201334 ms, with small intentional velocity accents. R4: final-third mid-pad entrances reduce from ten to two E2/D2 pedals, selected glass voices fall an octave, sparse lower bell answers expose Mara\u2019s phrase, and four highest climax bells soften by 2 dB. First 90 seconds and the 168\u2013192 second return retain exact score events.",
